.TH VAULT-GENKEY 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-genkey \- create a new vault key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault genkey
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates the key file, prompting twice for a passphrase, then for an optional
decoy passphrase (empty for none). Both passphrase slots are sealed with
Argon2id and XChaCha20-Poly1305, are the same size, and are stored in random
order; the second holds either a decoy identity or random bytes. It refuses to
overwrite an existing file. No seed or private key is ever written unencrypted.
.PP
When \fBVAULT_PASSPHRASE\fR is set, no prompts are made and the decoy comes
from \fBVAULT_DECOY_PASSPHRASE\fR, or is omitted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Where to write the key. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.TP
.B VAULT_DECOY_PASSPHRASE
Decoy passphrase; must differ from the passphrase.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-init (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
